{{Quote|That place&hellip; is strong with the dark side of the Force. A domain of evil it is. In you must go.''"<br />"''What's in there?''"<br />"''Only what you take with you.|[[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]] and [[Luke Skywalker/Legends|Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="ESB" />}}
The '''Cave of Evil''', also known as the '''Dark Side Cave''', was a cave on [[Dagobah/Legends|Dagobah]] containing a powerful [[Dark Spirit|dark-side manifestation of the Force]].

==Description==
A cave of limestone and dirt, the Dark Side Cave was located deep in the equatorial swamps and contained a [[Vergence/Legends|vergence]] in [[The Force/Legends|the Force]] as well as the apparition of a dark Jedi. A focal point for the [[Dark side of the Force/Legends|dark side of the Force]], the cave challenged the perceptions of anyone who entered into its depths. It drew visitors in, and they often experienced visions of the past, future, or possible futures.<ref name="NoP">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref>

==History==

===Origins===
In [[700 BBY]], the [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] [[Minch (Jedi)|Minch]] battled and killed a powerful [[Bpfasshi Dark Jedi leader]],<ref name="HOD" /> and his energies absorbed into its surroundings, tainting the passage<ref name="CSWE">{{CSWECite|II|315|Minch}}</ref> with the [[Dark Spirit]].<ref name="POTJ">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: Power of the Jedi|pack=Darth Vader (Dagobah)|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/potjdagvader.asp}}</ref>

===The Clone Wars===
[[File:Anidagobah.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Anakin and Qui-Gon visit the Dark Side Cave in Yoda's visions.]]
During the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]], [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]] had a vision of the Dark Side Cave during one of his meditations. In this vision, [[Qui-Gon Jinn/Legends|Qui-Gon Jinn]] had survived the [[Battle of Naboo/Legends|Battle of Naboo]] and had taken nine-year-old [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin Skywalker]] as his [[Padawan/Legends|Padawan]]. He guided Skywalker into the cave to face his fears, telling him the same thing Yoda eventually told Anakin's son, [[Luke Skywalker/Legends|Luke]], many years later, including telling Anakin that inside the cave was "only what you take with you."<ref name="CW">{{CW|21}}</ref>

Near the end of the Clone Wars, Yoda entered the cave under the guidance of Qui-Gon, who had learned how to speak from beyond. Here, Yoda had visions of the fall of the [[Jedi Order/Legends|Jedi Order]] and of the rise of [[Palpatine/Legends|Darth Sidious]].<ref name="Voices">{{TCW|Voices}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Brought you here, the galaxy has. Your path, clearly, this is.''"<br />"''You know what I'm looking for.''"<br />"''Something lost. A part of yourself, perhaps. That which you seek, inside, you will find.|Yoda and Galen Marek's clone|audio=SomethingLost-TFU2.flac|<ref name="TFU2">''[[Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II]]''</ref>}}
During the [[Great Jedi Purge/Legends|Great Jedi Purge]], Yoda realized that proximity to the Dark Side Cave could help neutralize his strong [[Light side of the Force/Legends|light-side]] Force signature&mdash;thus preventing his detection by the [[Sith/Legends|Sith]]&mdash;and took up residence near the cave, living there for the next two [[Standard decade/Legends|decades]], through the reign of the [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Galactic Empire]].<ref name="HTTE">''[[Heir to the Empire]]''</ref> Soon after the exile, an Imperial scout named [[Keog Boorn]] investigated a signal near the cave. A hidden Yoda saw how the scout left the place after remembering about the Bpfasshi Dark Jedi and hearing some terrifying sounds. Keog Boorn left the planet and reported that there was nothing on Dagobah, the signal just an atmospheric disturbance.<ref name="HttESB">''[[Heir to the Empire Sourcebook]]''</ref>

[[File:TheCave-SWGs7.jpg|thumb|180px|Yoda confronts the dark spirit taking the form of Darth Sidious in the cave]]
During the birth of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic/Legends|Rebellion]], the [[Subject 1138|clone of Starkiller]] spoke with Yoda briefly before entering the cave to look for the answers he sought. Inside, he was unable to use his Force powers, except for [[Mind trick/Legends|mind trick]], which he utilized several times. He faced the Dark Spirit who took the form of several [[Aberrant clone|other clones of Starkiller]] and had to carefully traverse some deep pits. He made it deep into the caves, and received a [[Force vision/Legends|vision]] of the [[Battle near the Itani Nebula|assault on the ''Salvation'']]. Starkiller exited the cave, and left the planet.<ref name="TFUII">''[[Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II]]''</ref>

In [[1 ABY/Legends|1 ABY]], the young [[Force-sensitive/Legends|Force-sensitive]] [[Zak Arranda/Legends|Zak Arranda]] accidentally led a [[The Children|group]] of [[Diet/Legends|cannibal]] [[Youngling/Legends|younglings]] into the Cave. The Dark Spirit tortured them reenacting scenes of their past, when their [[Parent/Legends|parents]] were forced to nourish them upon their own flesh.<ref name="Hunger">''[[Galaxy of Fear: The Hunger]]''</ref>

===Visits by Luke Skywalker===
[[File:DSC.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Luke revisits the cave in [[9 ABY/Legends|9 ABY]].]]
When Luke Skywalker traveled to Dagobah to train with Yoda in [[3 ABY/Legends|3 ABY]], the elder Master tasked him with entering the cave. Luke confronted<ref name="ESB" /> the Dark Spirit<ref name="POTJ" /> in the form of [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Darth Vader]] within and defeated it in a [[Lightsaber/Legends|lightsaber]] duel, dipping into the passion of the dark side in the process. There he realized what would happen if he turned to the dark side of the Force. Behind the mask of Darth Vader, he saw his own face. It also presaged the revelation that Vader was, unbeknownst to him at the time, his father, Anakin Skywalker.<ref name="ESB" />

[[9 ABY/Legends|Five years after Yoda's death]], Luke Skywalker returned to the cave. This time, he had a vision of a possible past, one where [[Mara Jade Skywalker|Mara Jade]] accompanied [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure/Legends|Jabba]] the [[Hutt/Legends|Hutt's]] retinue to the [[Sarlacc/Legends|sarlacc]]. She pulled Luke's lightsaber away from him when his vision suddenly ended. While in the cave, he found a beacon<ref name="HTTE" /> left behind by [[Jorj Car'das]].<ref name="VOTF">''[[Vision of the Future]]''</ref>

===Other visits===
In [[14 ABY/Legends|14 ABY]], the dark-side power of the cave was siphoned by the [[Disciples of Ragnos]]. This supposedly removed all of the dark energy,<ref name="JA">''[[Star Wars: Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy]]''</ref> but it presumably returned to its source when the [[Scepter of Ragnos]] was destroyed or otherwise somehow regenerated itself.<ref name="AQ">''[[Junior Jedi Knights: Anakin's Quest]]''</ref>

In [[22 ABY/Legends|22 ABY]], [[Anakin Solo]], [[Tahiri Veila]], and [[Uldir Lochett]] entered the cave after Anakin had a recurring nightmare of becoming the infamous Darth Vader. There, Tahiri encountered a vision of her parents and grandfather, and Anakin faced the manifestations of his own doubts. The two both emerged victorious. Uldir, who was not Force-sensitive, encountered nothing in the cave but vast emptiness.<ref name="AQ" />

Other Force-sensitive beings to enter the cave included [[Tash Arranda/Legends|Tash Arranda]] and Zak Arranda.<ref name="Hunger" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|No less has the passage of ''eight hundred years'' diminished the disquieting influence of the dark side.|[[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]]|<ref name="Star Wars Infinities: A New Hope">''[[Star Wars Infinities: A New Hope]]''</ref>}}
''[[Star Wars Infinities: A New Hope]]'', while under the [[Infinities]] label, establishes that the cave was tainted some eight hundred years before the [[Battle of Yavin/Legends|Battle of Yavin]].

[[File:Gnarltree-mcquarrie.jpg|thumb|200px|Concept art of Luke before entering the cave]]
''[[Vision of the Future]]'' describes how Yoda battled and defeated a powerful Bpfasshi Dark Jedi inside the Cave. But, in [[Star Wars Insider 98|''Star Wars Insider'' 98]], [[Leland Chee]] writes that this is no longer considered part of continuity because Yoda had never been on Dagobah before his exile. The concept of Yoda having never been on Dagobah prior to his exile was, in turn, later contradicted by "[[Voices]]," an installment of the CGI animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', which revealed that Yoda had, in fact, been to Dagobah, having been summoned there by the spirit of Qui-Gon Jinn to learn about the [[Force ghost/Legends|path to immortality]].

In ''Battlefront II''{{'s}} Dagobah map, the cave is one of several command posts; inside it, players can hear Darth Vader's distinctive breathing sound.

''The Story of Starkiller'', a video documentary about the ''[[Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II]]'' video game, revealed that the location's name is the Cave of Evil, as stated by project lead [[W. Haden Blackman|Haden Blackman]] and executive producer [[Julio Torres]].<ref name="Story">{{LucasArts|url=games/theforceunleashed2|text=''Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II''}} {{C|''The Story of Starkiller'' video documentary}}</ref>

The [[Gnarltree/Legends|gnarltree]] at the entrance to the cave is known as The Magic Tree, after the corresponding [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back Original Soundtrack|soundtrack]] cue.

